1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,040
 Hi, and this lesson I will talk about prompt engineering. Let's get started.

2
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:09,360
 Prompt engineering is the process of writing and refining instructions,

3
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:16,480
 so that AI tools like chat GPT, mid-journey, Gemini, and others give better answers.

4
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:23,200
 It is about finding the right way to ask, guide, and provide context, so the AI understands exactly

5
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:29,040
 what you want. If the AI's first answer is not what you need, you can adjust the prompt,

6
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:36,400
 add more details or rephrasing this way. The final result improves. A prompt is the instruction

7
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:43,920
 you give to an AI model. It can be something very simple like asking what is the capital of France,

8
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:51,920
 or it can be more complex with style format and context included such as write a short

9
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:57,200
 blog post in a friendly tone about why React is popular among developers.

10
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:02,400
 The clearer your prompt is, the better the AI's response will be.

11
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:08,800
 Prompt engineering is important because a well-structured prompt helps AI give relevant and accurate

12
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:14,400
 outputs. It reduced mistakes like wrong answers or off-topic results.

13
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:20,880
 It saves time by providing results that are already close to what you need without heavy editing.

14
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:27,360
 It also allows AI to handle complex tasks such as writing, coding, summarizing,

15
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:33,680
 and/or generating images more effectively. Prompt engineering is not about knowing AI in great depth.

16
00:01:33,680 --> 00:01:38,240
 Instead, it is about learning how to communicate with it clearly.

17
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:46,560
 Beginners can start with simple instructions. Advanced users can build detailed prompts that

18
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:54,000
 include roles, tone, and context. Just like coding, you get better with practice and feedback.

19
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:00,960
 Prompt engineering has many use cases. Writers use it to draft stories, blogs, or summaries.

20
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:06,080
 Developers use it for writing code, debugging, and documentation.

21
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:10,480
 Designers use it for generating and editing images.

22
00:02:10,480 --> 00:02:16,160
 Businesses use it for chatbots, data analysis, and automation.

23
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:21,040
 Students use it for learning, practice, and explanations.

24
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:26,000
 Prompts can take different forms, depending on the task.

25
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:30,960
 For language and text generation examples include creative writing,

26
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:36,400
 such as write a short story about a young woman who finds a portal in her attic.

27
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:42,000
 Summarization, like summarize this article in three bullet points.

28
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:47,040
 Translation, for instance, translate these texts from English to Spanish.

29
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:54,000
 Dialog such as your friendly chatbot helping a user fix their computer.

30
00:02:54,000 --> 00:03:02,640
 A question answering, prompts can be. Open ended such as explain quantum computing in simple

31
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:08,800
 words, specific like, what is the capital of France, multiple choice, for example,

32
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:16,320
 who wrote Harry Potter A, Tolkien B, Roland C, King. Hypothetical,

33
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:20,240
 like, what would happen if humans could travel at the speed of light.

34
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:26,720
 Opinion-based, such as, do you think AI will replace teachers, why or why not?

35
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:34,000
 For code generation prompts include, code completion, like write a Python function to calculate

36
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:39,760
 factorial. Code translation, such as convert this Python code to JavaScript.

37
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:45,840
 Optimization, for example, makes a SQL query faster, debugging,

38
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:51,840
 like fix the undefined in this JavaScript code. For image generation, prompts can be.

39
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:58,320
 Port realistic, such as a sunset over the ocean with form trees in front.

40
00:03:58,320 --> 00:04:05,520
 In an artistic style, like an impressionist painting of a rainy street with umbrellas,

41
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:11,440
 abstract, for example, an image representing hope using bright colors.

42
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:18,080
 Editing such as replace the background of this photo with a starry night sky.

43
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:24,320
 Here are the key takeaways. A prompt simply is the instruction you give to AI.

44
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:28,560
 Prompt engineering means shaping these instructions to get better answers.

45
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:34,880
 Clear and detailed prompts lead to more accurate, creative and useful results.

46
00:04:34,880 --> 00:04:40,400
 Anyone can learn this skill, practice and feedback will help you improve.

47
00:04:42,560 --> 00:04:48,960
 Good prompts unlock AI's full potential for writing, coding, design, learning and business.

48
00:04:48,960 --> 00:04:54,800
 I hope this lesson was useful for you and see you in the next lesson.

